### Starkvault File Upload Endpoints
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### Variables (update these as needed)
@testEmail = test@example.com
@testPassword = password123
@documentId = 507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
@arweaveHash = your_arweave_transaction_hash_here

### Prerequisites: Login first to get authentication cookie
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

###
### 1. Upload File to Arweave
### Note: Replace the file path with an actual file on your system
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123

--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test-document.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is a test document content for Arweave upload.
It contains some sample text to test the upload functionality.
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Test document for Arweave upload
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tags"

test,document,arweave
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="isPublic"

false
--boundary123--

###
### 2. Upload File with Minimal Data
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary456

--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="minimal-test.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Minimal test file content.
--boundary456--

###
### 3. Get User's Documents (with pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents

###
### 4. Get User's Documents with Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents?search=test&page=1&limit=5

###
### 5. Get User's Documents - Page 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents?page=2&limit=10

###
### 6. Get Document by ID
### Note: Replace {{documentId}} with actual document ID from upload response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/document/{{documentId}}

###
### 7. Get File from Arweave (proxy endpoint)
### Note: Replace {{arweaveHash}} with actual Arweave transaction hash
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file/{{arweaveHash}}

###
### 8. Check Arweave Transaction Status
### Note: Replace {{arweaveHash}} with actual Arweave transaction hash
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/status/{{arweaveHash}}

###
### 9. Delete Document from Database
### Note: Replace {{documentId}} with actual document ID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/document/{{documentId}}

###
### 10. Test Upload without Authentication (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary789

--boundary789
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="unauthorized-test.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This should fail without authentication.
--boundary789--

###
### 11. Test Upload without File (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary999

--boundary999
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Upload without file should fail
--boundary999--

###
### 12. Upload Public Document
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary111

--boundary111
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="public-document.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

This is a public document that can be accessed by others.
--boundary111
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Public test document
--boundary111
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tags"

public,test,shared
--boundary111
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="isPublic"

true
--boundary111--

###
### 13. Upload Large Description and Tags
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary222

--boundary222
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="detailed-document.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Document with detailed metadata for testing purposes.
--boundary222
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

This is a comprehensive test document with a very detailed description that includes multiple sentences and various information about the document's purpose, content, and intended use case for testing the Arweave upload functionality.
--boundary222
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tags"

comprehensive,detailed,metadata,testing,arweave,upload,functionality,document,storage,permanent
--boundary222
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="isPublic"

false
--boundary222--